	(text "Notes:  \n1) Reverse engineered from a physical unit.  Not a manufacturer drawing. All \n   signal names are the author's; DSI's designations are unknown\n2) SW1 is actually located on the front control panel, pictured here for completeness\n3) Silkscreening on the board was incomplete for some passives.  RX and CX references\n   were not identified on the silk screen, those references were assigned by me.\n4) On the original device, the purple wires and black wires were swapped.  Originally\n   GND was J1-8 & J1-9, while GND_24V was J1-2 & J1-3.  The logic board had these\n   as drawn in this schematic.  This appears to have been a design error from DSI.\n   Pin removal from housing requires AMP tool 305183 or equivalent."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
